# =============================================================================
# dsh-plugin-query-enhance - what must never enter this public repository
# =============================================================================
#
# The rule this file enforces, in one sentence: the published tree contains
# source code, tests, tooling and documentation, and nothing else.
#
# Concretely, the following are kept out, each for a stated reason:
#
#   1. internal planning notes  - they quote the directories of the machine they
#                                 were written on
#   2. runtime state            - anything produced by running the plugin or by
#                                 installing it into a profile
#   3. dependencies and builds  - reproducible from package.json, noise in a diff
#   4. credentials and env      - never, under any circumstance
#   5. editor and OS noise      - not part of the project
#
# `npm run verify-boundary` re-checks the tracked set against these rules and
# fails on anything that looks like a local absolute path or a secret. Run it
# before every push; a green run is the evidence that this file is complete.

# --- 1. internal planning notes ----------------------------------------------
# Written on one specific machine, so they name its directories. Keep the design
# locally, or rewrite it without machine paths, before publishing it.
/DESIGN.md
/docs/

# --- 2. runtime state --------------------------------------------------------
# This plugin writes nothing into its own directory: it has no configuration file
# and no settings page, and everything it reads comes from the Host. These
# patterns are a second line of defence against a hand-copied file.
/config.json
/config.local.json
/config.*.json
/secrets.json
/plugin-data/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# --- 3. dependencies, builds, lockfiles --------------------------------------
# Installation is owned by DSH's `install_bundle` (pnpm). A second, npm-authored
# lockfile here would only describe a different resolver and create drift.
node_modules/
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
.npm/
.pnpm-store/
coverage/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- 4. credentials and local environment ------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.kdbx
.credentials.yaml
credentials.json
secrets.yaml

# --- 5. editor and OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store

# --- 6. local scratch and backups --------------------------------------------
# Profile backups and rollback material produced while installing the bundle.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej
/.dsh-tmp/
/tmp/
